{
  "question": "What is the New York City small purchase limit?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "The New York City small purchase limit is $100,000. This limit applies to procurements of goods and services, with a separate threshold for construction. The rule is established by the New York City Procurement Policy Board (PPB) Rules.",
